// When the left operand is false, `JumpIfFalse` jumps straight to the
// statement's `Pop`, which then discards that operand. The `Pop` follows the
// load of the right operand, `false`, but it's a jump target, so the pair must
// stay: removing it would leave the jump nowhere to land. The optimized code is
// the same as the raw.
// compile: parsed, parsed optimized
true and false;
